# working files created by status.py
agents.json.lock
agents.json.lock.d/
agents.json.tmp.*

# The channel's memory is COMMITTED, not ignored. niche.json is the one
# commitment the agents read before they choose anything; clips_used.json is
# the record of which footage has already been published, and an agent that
# cannot see it will re-cut the same film. performance.json is what actually
# worked. All three have to survive a fresh checkout or the agents start blind:
#   niche.json  clips_used.json  performance.json  sources.csv

# local run state — regenerable from the inputs, so not worth committing
# review/ holds finished Shorts waiting for a human: the text files are small
# but final.mp4 is not, and a repository is the wrong place to queue video.
review/
schedule_state.json
performance.md
performance-etsy.md
shop-niche.md
render.json
voice/
voice.wav
suppliers.json
products.json
promo.md
out/
assets/

# OAuth credentials — never commit these
client_secret.json
youtube_token.json
etsy_token.json

node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
